      "writtenOn": "2025-04-09T12:18:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I left comments for this on the code.\n\nWhat we want to do is\n\nif (removed IP address presents on multiple networks) {\n  if (there is no VPN) {\n    //exemptedNetIds are for the networks not losing this address.\n    destroy(address, Range(netid_min,netid_max), exemptedNetIds, null, mask);\n  } else if (all are VPN) {\n    // uidRange is for the network losing this address.\n    destroy(address, Range(netid_min,netid_max), null, uidRange, mask);\n  } else {\n    // If there are VPN and nonVPN mixed, delete all sockets for the address.\n    destroy(address, Range(netid_min,netid_max), null, null, mask);\n  }\n} else {\n  destroy(address, Range(netid_min,netid_max), null, null, mask);\n}\n\nDuring the design discussion, we recognize that it\u0027s too complex to determine which sockets to be destroyed if there are both VPN and nonVPN networks possessing the same IP address, So we concluded to destroy all sockets for the address at this case. It\u0027s not a regression as Netd currently does this.",
      "parentUuid": "6aac0d97_0fc67494",
